# Export allowlist template for macOS plugin dylibs — the Mach-O counterpart
# of plugin_exports.map.in, configured per target by pj_harden_plugin_exports().
# Entries are ld64 -exported_symbols_list patterns (leading underscore, '*'
# wildcards allowed); patterns that match nothing are ignored.
#
# Restricting exports is not just hygiene here: an exported weak C++ symbol
# (typeinfo, inline/template instantiation) participates in dyld's process-wide
# weak coalescing when the plugin is dlopen'd, so SOME of the plugin's
# references get rebound to the host executable's copy while archive-internal
# references keep their own. libc++ compares typeid by POINTER, so that split
# breaks RTTI identity inside the plugin (std::any resolving to "unknown type",
# any_cast failing). Keeping every non-ABI symbol local makes the plugin's
# statically linked C++ self-consistent, exactly like a plain executable.
_pj_plugin_abi_version
_PJ_get_data_source_vtable
_PJ_get_message_parser_vtable
_PJ_get_toolbox_vtable
_PJ_get_dialog_vtable
_pj_plugin_descriptor_*
@PJ_EXTRA_EXPORT_LINES@
